title: Welcome
card: Fathom | Learning the language | Every part of it, from the first line to a game of your own
say:
  Welcome to Fathom, a programming language that reads like English.
  In this film we'll go through every part of the language: what each piece does, and how to use it.
  At the end, we'll make a whole platform game together, and take it apart to see how it works.
uncard

say: This is Fathom Studia, where we'll write everything. Let's take a quick look around.
point: #files
say: On the left are the files in our folder. Programs are files whose names end in dot fathom.
point: #word-search
say: Below them is a list of every word the language knows. You can search it, and click a word to see what it does.
point: #run
say:
  Across the top are the buttons that do things with a program.
  Run runs it. Watch runs it one line at a time. Test runs its checks. Build makes it into a program of its own, and Web makes it into a web page.
point: #output
say: And at the bottom, this is where a program's words appear when it runs.
hide cursor

card: Chapter 1 | Saying something | Your first program
say: Every program starts somewhere. Let's write the smallest one.
uncard

new: hello.fathom
type:
  genesis:
    scrawl "Hello!"
  and the universe said i love you
zoom: lines 1-3
spot: line 1
say:
  The word genesis, with a colon, is where every program begins.
spot: line 2
say:
  The lines that belong to it are moved to the right, with two spaces. This one says scrawl, which shows something on the screen.
  Text goes between quote marks.
spot: line 3
say:
  And every block ends with this line: and the universe said I love you. It tells Fathom that genesis is finished.
spot: off
zoom: out
say: Let's run it.
run
zoom: output
say: There it is. Hello.
wait
zoom: out

say: Now something a little more useful. Text can have names inside it, in square brackets.
clear
type:
  genesis:
    set name to "Sam"
    set coins to 3
    scrawl "Hello, [name]! You have [coins] coins."
    scrawl "After this one, you'll have [coins plus 1]."
  and the universe said i love you
zoom: lines 2-5
spot: lines 2-3
say:
  Set name to Sam remembers the text Sam under the name: name.
  And coins remembers the number three.
spot: line 4
say: Inside the quote marks, square brackets are filled in with whatever the words in them hold.
spot: line 5
say: And they can even work things out, like coins plus one.
spot: off
run
zoom: output
say: Hello Sam, you have three coins. After this one, you'll have four.
wait
zoom: out
